# Containers on the desktop (docs/containers.md): where the browser makes a tab, it makes it in
# its container (src/chrome/browser/containers/platform/). dubna's containers.patch has the hooks
# tennessine shares.
# - chrome_command_ids.h: the command ids of the container submenus.
# - browser_navigator.cc: a new tab that a page opens without an opener (a link opened in a new
#   tab, from the page or its context menu) starts in the page's container.
# - browser_tabrestore.cc: a restored tab, after a restart or reopened, starts in the container
#   its session saved.
# - browser_tabstrip.cc: a new tab opens in the container Settings says (brave-core#40693).
# - startup_tab.h, pinned_tab_codec.cc, startup_browser_creator_impl.cc: pinned tabs, which open
#   at startup without the session when Settings says to open the new tab page, keep their
#   container too: one in a container opens now, not deferred without it.
# - browser_commands.cc (Alt+Enter in the address bar), browser_root_view.cc (a link dropped on
#   the tab strip): a new tab opens in the active tab's container.
